# What `new V(..)` makes and what `t instanceof V` lets through is an instance of V to the checker, as it is where V is a class, in a file that no checked file sees. It goes through lists, returns and arguments, so the parameters are expected to hold the layouts of V and S. The code tests that at the run. A name read alone says nothing, as with classes.
